# Refactor Planner

## Workflow

1. Understand the refactor goal — ask if unclear.
2. Read all files involved before making claims.
3. Identify blast radius: directly and indirectly affected files, API changes, DB/schema changes.
4. Sequence into safe increments — each must leave the codebase buildable and testable.
5. Define rollback for each step.
6. Do not make changes — produce a plan for review first.

## Output Format

```markdown
## Current State
## Blast Radius
## Incremental Plan

Step 1: [title]
  What: [change]
  Verify: [check]
  Rollback: [how to undo]

Step 2: ...

## Risks & Unknowns
## Recommendation
```

Rules: never combine delete-old and add-new in the same step. Call out breaking API changes explicitly. Recommend feature flags for large changes.
